From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] dwrite: font set queries, filters and builder additions

Font sets listed their fonts and little else; everything past that was
E_NOTIMPL (Office, WinUI and Chromium-based text stacks ask these):

- fonts answer their weight, stretch and style properties as decimal
  strings (the names' differentiation rules and simulations applied, as
  for the font objects);
- GetPropertyValues lists a property's values over the whole set, or per
  preferred locale, as an IDWriteStringList;
- GetPropertyOccurrenceCount counts the fonts with a value;
- matching and filtering take every property id; GetMatchingFonts by
  family, weight, stretch and style gives the family's fonts nearest
  first (style, then stretch, then weight);
- FindFontFaceReference and FindFontFace find a font in the set;
- IDWriteFontSet1: GetMatchingFonts by property, GetFirstFontResources,
  GetFilteredFonts by indices and by properties (all or any),
  GetFilteredFontIndices, GetFontFaceReference and CreateFontFace;
- the builder adds font sets, face references with properties of their
  own, and fonts (AddFont); a collection made from a set takes the family
  and face names the set gave a font.

Wine's dwrite font tests: four todo_wine marks removed (the weight,
stretch and style properties exist; AddFontFaceReference with properties;
the collection holds the given family), no new failures (the four
refcount/todo results from 0503 are as before).

Gate: test/fontquery-gate.sh (64- and 32-bit). Mutants
SG_MUTANT_NO_FONTSET_PROPERTIES, SG_MUTANT_NO_FONTSET_METHODS,
SG_MUTANT_NO_FONT_DISTANCE, SG_MUTANT_NO_GIVEN_NAMES (dwrite/font.c).
